2.	Scope 
State Business Need or Issue:
Currently, the MA21 system sends out a blank renewal form for members, when it is time for renewal. This process does not leverage existing verified data available within MA21.The business requires the ability to generate a Prepopulated Renewal Form (PPF) containing available verified member and household data to improve accuracy, efficiency, and member experience.
How it works now or the cause:
At present, when a member’s renewal period arrives, MA21 identifies the case and triggers the Common Noticing Solution (CNS) to generate    a cover letter and the print vendor inserts a blank renewal form.and send a blank renewal form.
1.	The current process does not extract or include any pre-existing data elements listed in each of the Data Areas identified in the business provided PPF template.
2.	As a result, members must manually fill in all fields on the form, leading to incomplete or inconsistent data submissions.
How it will work:
After implementation, MA21 will build a process to generate and transmit Prepopulated Form (PPF) data elements to CNS through the existing CNS integration process.
1.	When members fall under the paper renewal path, MA21 will compile data elements listed in each of the Data Areas identified in the business-provided PPF template. verified   data available in its system across the data elements listed in each of the Data Areas identified in the business provided PPF template and include it in the PPF payload.  
1.2.	This includes member and household information sourced from applicable MA21 subsystems based on availability and eligibility for prepopulation.
2.3.	MA21 will send this structured data to CNS, which will render and print the renewal form with prepopulated member details.
3.4.	This ensures members receive a renewal form that already contains known and verified   information, requiring them only to review and update changes if needed.
4.5.	For auto-renewal path members, MA21 will not send PPF data for printing and mailing.The PPF may still be generated and made viewable in MyServices with the associated cover letter, consistent with current HIX behavior. to CNS, as those renewals are handled automatically  .
Comments:
1.	MA21 will follow the data elements listed in each of the Data Areas identified in the business provided PPF template.
2.	Please look into Appendix B for the PrePopulated Template
3.	Additional Business Requirements (Masking/Conditional Data):
	Apply masking for sensitive identifiers on the PPF when rendered (e.g., partial masking with Xs as shown in business sample).
	Conditionally populate and send certain data elements only when the preceding question response is 'Yes' per business rules.
 
2.1	Use Case Scenarios
U30179 - 01 Goal – Generate Prepopulated Renewal Form (PPF)
Person Actors:  Members   (ARDs), PSIs receive the cover letter only.
Prepopulated Renewal Forms are generated for ARDs only. PSIs do not receive the PPF and will receive only the associated cover letter.
System Actors:  MA21 System & CNS
Pre-Conditions: 
1.	MA21 Member Renewal is due.
2.	Member is on the paper renewal path.
3.	Member Verified data exists in MA21 for relevant data elements listed in each of the Data Areas identified in the business provided PPF template.
4.	MA21 and CNS integration is functional.
Main Flow:
1.	MA21 identifies the member due for renewal   and determines the applicable renewal selection type (paper renewal (or) auto-renewal).
2.	MA21 checks that the member follows the paper renewal path.
3.	MA21 gathers  available verified member data elements listed in each of the Data Areas identified in the business provided PPF template.
4.	MA21 formats the data according to the CNS schema/mapping for the PPF payload.
5.	MA21 sends the PPF payload to CNS through the integration process.
6.	CNS receives the payload and renders the prepopulated renewal form using the CNS template.
7.	CNS renders the Prepopulated Renewal Form and delivers it according to delivery preferences, including print, mail, electronic delivery and worker copies as applicable. prints   and Mail the PPF to the member  
7.8.	CNS mails or electronically delivers the Prepopulated Renewal Form to ARDs only and PSIs receive the cover letter without the PPF.
Alternate Flow #:
1.	If some data elements are missing, MA21 sends only available data elements listed in each of the Data Areas identified in the business provided PPF template.
2.	CNS generates form with prepopulated fields where data exists, When CNS Shows no data available Then, member manually completes missing fields.
Exception Flow #:
1.	MA21 identifies member is on auto-renewal path.
2.	No PPF payload is sent to CNS.
3.	MA21 marks renewal as auto-processed, no paper form is generated.
Post Success Condition:
1.	Member receives a prepopulated renewal form with all available verified data filled in.
2.	CNS successfully logs the PPF generation event.


U30179 - 02 Goal - Mask and Conditionally Populate PPF Data Elements
Person Actors:   Members
System Actors:  MA21 System & CNS
Pre-Conditions:  
1.	Member is on the paper   renewal path and is due for renewal and has been identified as following the paper renewal selection path..
2.	MA21 has available verified data for one or more PPF data elements.
3.	Business rules identify which fields must be masked and which are conditional based on preceding questions.
4.	MA21→CNS integration for PPF payload is available.
Main Flow:
1.	MA21 assembles PPF data elements per template/mapping/schema.
2.	For each sensitive field, MA21 applies the required masking rule before placing the value in the CNS payload (e.g., show only permitted digits/characters and mask remaining characters).
3.	For each conditional section, MA21 evaluates the preceding question:
	If the preceding question is answered “Yes”, MA21 includes the dependent follow-up data elements (if verified/available).
	If the preceding question is answered “No”, MA21 does not include the dependent follow-up data elements (CNS should display them as blank/not applicable).
4.	MA21 transmits the masked/conditional PPF payload to CNS.
5.	CNS renders the PPF using the CNS template and prints/mails the form.
Alternate Flow #:
1.	If a conditional question is “Yes” but dependent data is not available/verified, MA21 sends the section with ‘No Data Available’/blank values as applicable, while still honoring masking rules
Exception Flow #:
1.	If the member is on the auto-renewal path, MA21 does not send the PPF payload to CNS.
Post Success Condition:
1.	Member receives a PPF where sensitive fields are masked and conditional sections appear only when applicable.
2.	MA21 logs payload generation and any masking/conditional rule application outcomes for audit/traceability.

3.	Functional Requirements 
Describe from a users perspective, the functions that the system is required to perform.
Functional Requirement  Number	Detailed Functional Requirement.  

J30179 – 01 - A	Generate Prepopulated Renewal Form (PPF): The system must generate a prepopulated renewal form for members who follow the paper renewal path, using verified   data available in MA21.
J30179 – 01 - B	Identify Eligible Members: MA21 must   identify members due for renewal and determine if they are on the paper renewal path. Only these members will receive the prepopulated form.

J30179 – 01- C	ARD and PSI Handling: MA21 must generate and send Prepopulated Renewal Forms only for ARDs. PSIs must receive only the associated cover letter and no PPF data
J30179 – 01- DC	Payload Creation for CNS: MA21 must format and send verifie  d member data to CNS according to the agreed PPF Template, Schema and mapping, ensuring all Prepopulated fields are accurately filled if available.

J30179 – 01- ED	Partial Data Handling: If only partial verified data is available, MA21 must still generate the PPF payload for CNS, prepopulating only available fields. Members should manually complete any missing information.

J30179 – 01- FE	Exception Handling: If a member is on the auto-renewal path or is identified as a PSI, MA21 must not send PPF payload data to CNS for printing and mailing., MA21 should not send PPF payload Data  .

J30179 – 01- GF	Audit and Logging: MA21 must log each PPF generation event, including member ID, payload details, and timestamp, to ensure traceability and support reporting/audit requirements.
J30179 – 01- HG	Integration Verification: MA21 must include the appropriate CNS insert group number within the payload to support print integration. MA21 will coordinate with the CNS team to obtain and configure the correct insert group number. MA21   must ensure that CNS receives the payload successfully and can render the prepopulated form without errors. Any failures should trigger error handling or alerts.
J30179 – 02 - A	Masking & Conditional Data Rules: MA21 must apply business-defined masking rules for sensitive data elements and conditionally include or omit dependent data elements in the PPF payload based on preceding question responses (e.g., only send follow-up values when the controlling question is 'Yes').


